1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:03,272
First stop:

2
00:00:03,572 --> 00:00:05,617
a company the coffee shop pays

3
00:00:05,617 --> 00:00:06,980
to handle its cards.

4
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:09,770
It works for the shop, not for ZERO.

5
00:00:10,170 --> 00:00:12,426
And it has no idea who he is.

6
00:00:13,276 --> 00:00:15,201
It only reads the first digits

7
00:00:15,201 --> 00:00:16,420
of the card number.

8
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:18,760
They say which network to ask,

9
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,368
and which bank is behind the card.

10
00:00:22,868 --> 00:00:24,740
Which raises a better question.

11
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:27,272
Why does a coffee need a network at all?

12
00:00:28,968 --> 00:00:31,584
Because thousands of banks issue cards,

13
00:00:31,884 --> 00:00:33,948
and millions of shops take them.

14
00:00:34,098 --> 00:00:35,850
Most of them have never met.

15
00:00:36,250 --> 00:00:37,952
The network is where they

16
00:00:37,952 --> 00:00:39,178
all agree to meet,

17
00:00:39,578 --> 00:00:41,450
under one set of rules.

18
00:00:42,100 --> 00:00:44,235
In the U.S., that's mostly

19
00:00:44,235 --> 00:00:45,796
Visa or Mastercard.

20
00:00:46,096 --> 00:00:48,643
In a single year, Visa alone

21
00:00:48,643 --> 00:00:51,280
handled 258 billion payments.

22
00:00:51,680 --> 00:00:54,248
That's about eight thousand every second.

23
00:00:55,648 --> 00:00:57,522
All of it runs through four

24
00:00:57,522 --> 00:00:58,840
giant data centers,

25
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:00,484
with spare power,

26
00:01:00,734 --> 00:01:02,606
spare cooling

27
00:01:02,756 --> 00:01:04,628
and spare connections,

28
00:01:04,778 --> 00:01:07,010
so a question never has to wait.

29
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:13,232
Here's the strange part.

30
00:01:13,532 --> 00:01:15,716
The network doesn't move money either.

31
00:01:15,916 --> 00:01:17,788
It moves questions.

32
00:01:19,188 --> 00:01:21,468
Last stop: ZERO's bank.

33
00:01:21,768 --> 00:01:23,640
The one that gave him the card.

34
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:25,761
It has a fraction of a second

35
00:01:25,761 --> 00:01:27,152
to answer two things.

36
00:01:27,552 --> 00:01:29,424
Does he have enough credit?

37
00:01:29,824 --> 00:01:31,696
And is this really him?

38
00:01:32,446 --> 00:01:35,230
For the second one, it doesn't ask ZERO.

39
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:37,114
It asks his habits.

40
00:01:37,414 --> 00:01:40,258
Visa says its own system weighs more than

41
00:01:40,258 --> 00:01:43,102
five hundred details about every payment,

42
00:01:43,502 --> 00:01:45,374
in about a millisecond.

43
00:01:45,924 --> 00:01:48,132
But ZERO's card is brand new.

44
00:01:48,432 --> 00:01:49,944
He has no habits.

45
00:01:50,244 --> 00:01:52,116
And to a fraud machine,

46
00:01:52,516 --> 00:01:54,125
no history can look a lot

47
00:01:54,125 --> 00:01:55,348
like a stolen card.

48
00:01:56,624 --> 00:01:58,280
Back in the coffee shop,

49
00:01:58,580 --> 00:02:01,076
the clock says one point one seconds.

50
00:02:01,626 --> 00:02:03,501
If a bank ever takes too

51
00:02:03,501 --> 00:02:04,986
long, or goes down,

52
00:02:05,286 --> 00:02:07,158
the network can answer for it,

53
00:02:07,258 --> 00:02:08,986
using AI to stand in.

54
00:02:09,086 --> 00:02:11,174
But ZERO's bank isn't down.

55
00:02:11,674 --> 00:02:13,018
It's just not sure.

56
00:02:13,768 --> 00:02:15,424
Then the evidence adds up.

57
00:02:15,724 --> 00:02:17,596
A real chip,

58
00:02:17,996 --> 00:02:20,228
one only the real card can make.

59
00:02:20,328 --> 00:02:22,200
A tiny amount.

60
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:24,269
A coffee shop a few blocks

61
00:02:24,269 --> 00:02:25,360
from his address.

62
00:02:26,310 --> 00:02:28,182
Credit: yes.

63
00:02:28,482 --> 00:02:29,875
And now look at what the

64
00:02:29,875 --> 00:02:30,978
bank actually does.

65
00:02:31,378 --> 00:02:33,250
It doesn't send any money.

66
00:02:33,550 --> 00:02:35,952
It puts a hold on four seventy-five

67
00:02:35,952 --> 00:02:37,462
of ZERO's credit line.

68
00:02:37,762 --> 00:02:39,634
A promise.

69
00:02:41,034 --> 00:02:43,194
And the promise works both ways.

70
00:02:43,494 --> 00:02:45,366
If the coffee never showed up,

71
00:02:45,766 --> 00:02:47,806
ZERO could dispute the charge,

72
00:02:47,906 --> 00:02:49,443
and the money would be pulled

73
00:02:49,443 --> 00:02:50,450
back from the shop.

74
00:02:51,534 --> 00:02:53,742
The answer rides back the same way.

75
00:02:54,042 --> 00:02:54,858
Bank,

76
00:02:55,158 --> 00:02:56,118
network,

77
00:02:56,318 --> 00:02:58,190
the shop's company,

78
00:02:58,390 --> 00:03:00,262
the terminal.

79
00:03:01,562 --> 00:03:03,434
Two seconds.

80
00:03:05,262 --> 00:03:06,990
ZERO thinks he just paid.

81
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:08,226
He didn't.

82
00:03:08,726 --> 00:03:10,670
Nobody has paid anybody.

83
00:03:11,170 --> 00:03:13,042
Not yet.

84
00:03:13,342 --> 00:03:15,598
So when does the money actually move?
